{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$g : \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$g \\circ f$", "MATH_0004": "$g$", "MATH_0005": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-presentation-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8e65fd2cd4516bb493f477762093f251a5b08595dc790e695f999360969dcc5e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2b69f83fbef304d7f45ead73961d6e0ff0725310923d7a074bb8a280b1914766", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and\n<MATH_0002> be morphisms of algebraic stacks\nIf <MATH_0003> is locally of finite presentation and <MATH_0004> is locally of\nfinite type, then <MATH_0005> is locally of finite presentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f4c5048f0f78848f7bd43fe6085d42375b5551dbfe4b4f9caeb6badba856ee2d", "unit_id": "tag:06Q6:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$W$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Y} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} W$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} V$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to V \\to W$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-finite-presentation-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c274a87eee0758921bbef94dcca1b895728509e71308430edd333df88794986a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0d28d5882e0fad2f6d71f5376c1ca694e78270086832530c2704e3a9721007c0", "source_text": "Choose an algebraic space <MATH_0001> and a surjective smooth morphism\n<MATH_0002>.\nChoose an algebraic space <MATH_0003> and a surjective smooth morphism\n<MATH_0004>.\nChoose an algebraic space <MATH_0005> and a surjective smooth morphism\n<MATH_0006>.\nThe lemma follows upon applying\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>\nto the morphisms <MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f0b0c00273f98cf76153184ab6821b75fb8256fad261ac3bc48aa623d97906b5", "unit_id": "tag:06Q6:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-diagonal-morphism-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dba23b97bcaab97303499f7cafeb7fb157c409b5d676bb146a9f13f531188c7e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fcd8817b0ea333f05f555a6f4a2654798598c0bf5a6e794a4e02a9cf83e39f42", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks\nwith diagonal\n<MATH_0002>.\nIf <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type then <MATH_0004> is\nlocally of finite presentation. If <MATH_0005> is\nquasi-separated and locally of finite type, then <MATH_0006> is of finite\npresentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3d63bdb08acd3ab39a0dbc34d5777439cdcde7f00fae38411e2b00a835255b4d", "unit_id": "tag:0CMG:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Delta$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\text{pr}_2 : \\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$f$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Delta_f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-finite-type}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-finite-presentation-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b3511d389a1e47f293f507a7ca40ef45e87cdbd0c64b713538bd91d979e366c5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:308152e13625f5616f4bb54fff4a1105d4e8577a54716dc3fe0e2dc8400717ae", "source_text": "Note that <MATH_0001> is a morphism over <MATH_0002> (via the second\nprojection). If <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type, then\n<MATH_0004> is of finite presentation over <MATH_0005> and\n<MATH_0006>\nis locally of finite type by Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThus the first statement holds by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nThe second statement follows from the first and\nthe definitions (because <MATH_0007> being quasi-separated means\nby definition that <MATH_0008> is quasi-compact and quasi-separated).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:09443729d028c939ce72f7a5a298e09d4eb99d96e3b0abf42f6eb7a7fefb2eaa", "unit_id": "tag:0CMG:proof"}
